{"kind":"assert","text":"Fresh restatement of the MCP unusable-resident policy decision, replacing a8477760, which went ordinarily stale through the merge-assert cascade while its substance is unchanged: the code it rules on has not moved (the late-actor lane is still unmerged), and hugh asked for a non-stale record to ratify. It carries no rests_on because every record in its provenance chain is stale and the relevant paths have no fresh artifact; the evidence is restated here in full. THE DECISION. cmd/gitseq-mcp must fail closed on a present-but-untrustworthy resident.json for durable writes, matching gs. (1) Missing record: unchanged — absence is the only reading meaning no resident; local operation stays the baseline. (2) Unusable record, including a published record whose URL fails validation: state, ratify and supersede refuse with an error naming the reason and the recovery, appending nothing to either log. Today endpoint() collapses AdvertisementUnusable into no-resident (cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go:166) and submit() folds durable acts locally with only degraded:true — the silent-custody hole the de274aac repair closed for gs, still open in the adapter; the code comment justifying it (main.go:153-160, no channel to refuse on) is wrong on its own terms because every tool call returns a per-call result, and a tool error is the refusal channel. (3) Reads (status, wait, work, artifacts, inspect, whoami) may keep answering from the verified local fold — deliberate divergence from gs, because a labeled local read misleads nobody and blinding the session blocks diagnosis — but must carry the unusable reason, never plain no-resident. (4) presence, say and ack already fail without a resident; with an unusable record their error names the reason. (5) Recovery: endpoint() already re-reads resident.json per call while no address is cached, so fixing or deleting the record takes effect on the next call without restart; keep that, and add a --local launch flag mirroring gs --server - (the retired --server flag stays retired). (6) Transport failure with a trustworthy record keeps the documented degraded fallback; out of scope here. COMPATIBILITY: valid-advertisement and no-advertisement sessions unchanged; only sessions over a corrupt record change, from silent local fold to explicit refusal. ARCHITECTURE: layers 3 and 7; the implementing head updates architecture.md:256-259, docs/reference/gs/serve.md:114-118, docs/reference/gs/status.md:249-253 and the main.go comment. TESTS: an unusable-class table on the MCP side mirroring cmd/gs/invalid_advertisement_test.go:83-179; per-tool refusal tests asserting the reason is named and depth unchanged in both logs; unusable-then-fixed recovery on the next call without restart; a --local test over a corrupt record. SEQUENCING: implementation only as a child request after the late-actor lane merges, on then-current cmd/gitseq-mcp and internal/app bases, citing this decision and hugh ratification."}